    "badge": "Best Overall",
    "description": "The Bosch GLL3-330CG throws a green beam all the way around the room in three directions: a level plane plus two plumb planes crossing at 90 degrees. Set it in the middle of a room and it paints a level line around every wall plus two plumb lines that cross on the ceiling and floor, which gives you square reference for cabinets, framing, tile and drop ceilings without moving the tool. Green beams appear noticeably brighter to the eye than red, so the lines stay readable in rooms with windows. The model runs on Bosch's 12-volt battery platform and also ships with an alkaline adapter on many kits. Bosch lists an accuracy of about plus or minus three thirty-seconds of an inch at 30 feet and a working range of up to roughly 330 feet with a compatible receiver, which is where the model number comes from. It includes a positioning device on many kits for fine adjustment, and owners commonly praise the beam brightness. The price is high for a homeowner who only hangs shelves.",
