    "description": "The DW089LG is DeWalt's three-plane green laser, and its biggest selling point is power. It runs on DeWalt's 12-volt MAX batteries and, on current versions, accepts 20-volt MAX packs as well, so anyone already on the yellow platform has a battery that lasts a full day. The three planes give level and two plumb references around the room. DeWalt rates it for jobsite abuse, with an overmolded housing and an ingress protection rating against dust and water spray, and its integrated magnetic pivoting base mounts to steel studs and track. Accuracy is listed at about 1/8 inch over 30 feet, slightly looser than the Bosch. Owners commonly mention that the beams are bright and the tool shrugs off drops that would trouble lighter lasers. It is heavier than consumer models and priced like a professional tool. If you already own DeWalt batteries, it is the easy choice among three-plane lasers.",
