            Most homeowners should start with a compact self-leveling cross-line, red if the budget is tight and the rooms are dim, green if they are bright. That single tool handles shelves, art, televisions and trim faster than any spirit level. The Bosch GLL55 and Klein 93LCLS are dependable choices.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Move to a three-plane green laser such as the Huepar 903CG, Bosch GLL3-330CG or DeWalt DW089LG when you take on cabinets, tile, framing or ceilings, and to a rotary kit like the Johnson for outdoor grading. Whatever you buy, keep it off when moving, mark one edge of the line consistently, and check it against two walls after any drop.
          </p>
